    <string name="anisette_upgrade_title">Sign in without a middleman</string>
    <string name="anisette_upgrade_message">Signing in to Apple currently goes through a public Anisette server. Its operator can see that traffic, and OpenTagViewer stops being able to sign in whenever their server is down.

This can now happen entirely on your phone instead. Switching means signing in one more time, because Apple treats it as a new device.</string>
